    path_color: one color != bg; most frequent non-bg color; forms a thick meandering diagonal band dividing the grid
    cycle_colors: 2-4 distinct-or-repeating colors, all != bg and != path_color
    end_color: one color, != bg, != path_color, != any cycle color
  template:
    location: top-left, one row of 2x2 monochrome blocks
    row_start: 1 or 2
    col_start: 1 (blocks occupy cols 1-2, 4-5, 7-8, 10-11 with stride 3)
    count: 2-4 2x2 blocks (defines the cycle, left-to-right)
    separator: bg-colored column between adjacent blocks
  end_block:
    shape: single 2x2 monochrome block of end_color
    location: in the bottom-right bg region (on the opposite side of path from template)
    constraint: all 4 cells must be bg in ambient, isolated from path
  markers:
    count: 1 or 2 isolated pixels (n_markers==2 in >=50% of samples)
    color: always equals the first template block's color (cycle_colors[0])
    location: column 0 (left grid edge); embedded in a col-0 path_region segment — i.e., (r,0) was path before painting; vertical neighbors (r-1,0) and (r+1,0) are also path
  path_region:
    shape: thick meandering diagonal band, spans full height and full width
    width_per_row: varies 2 to grid_width (wider in middle)
    topology: single 4-connected component of path_color that touches both the right/top edge and the bottom/left edge
    bg_components: path splits bg into 2-4 4-connected regions (top-left region holds template; bottom-right region holds end_block); when n_markers==2, typically >=3 components (the 3rd is a separator that isolates the two marker channels) [observed, test[0] is an exception with 2 markers and 2 components]
    separator: >-
      when n_markers==2, the separator is typically (~3/4) a NARROW (2-3 cells wide), ELONGATED bg
      strip that bites in from the left edge (col 0) and extends upper-right-ward roughly
      parallel to the path band's anti-diagonal direction, separating the trajectories of the two markers.
      It may alternatively (~1/4) be a fully-enclosed interior bg island, also elongated along the anti-diagonal.
      In both cases, the path region must not be cut off by the separator (maintain single 4-connected component).
  trajectory_constraints:
    per_marker_steps: 15-50 path cells traversed
    per_marker_turns: 0-4 (>=1 example has a marker with 0 turns; most have 2-4)
    total_turns_across_markers: >=3 (path should have enough meandering to force multiple collisions)
    initial_direction: first adjacent path cell in priority order R,D,L,U (for left-edge markers this is always Right)
    turn_rule: alternate CCW(left), CW(right), CCW, CW...; if scheduled turn is not path, particle stops
    disjoint_trajectories: when n_markers == 2, the two markers' visited path-cell sets must be disjoint (no overlap or crossing)
  output_transform:
    - erase all template 2x2 blocks to bg
    - erase the end 2x2 block to bg
    - for each marker: walk path, recoloring visited path cells by advancing cycle index starting from marker's own color
    - on each collision (non-path cell scheduled), paint that cell with end_color (a single-pixel corner marker)

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Pick H=W ∈ [20,30]; bg, path_color, end_color, 2-4 cycle_colors (all distinct).
    2. Pick n_markers ∈ {1,2} (~1:1) and marker rows at col 0:
      - n_markers=1: any row r in bottom half of col 0.
      - n_markers=2: r1<r2 with r2-r1>=4.
    3. Build the path band as a thick meandering anti-diagonal region (width 4-12, single 4-connected, touches {top,right} and {bottom,left} edges), enclosing all markers in col 0.
    4. Separator (n_markers=2 only): carve a narrow (2-3 cells wide) bg strip from col 0 starting between r1 and r2, extending rightward with up-right slope; top and bottom edges roughly parallel (do NOT taper to a 1-cell tip). Alternative (~1/4): enclosed interior island with same elongation.
    5. Place template: template_row ∈ {1,2}, 2-4 2x2 blocks at cols {1,4,7,10}[:n_markers], all bg pre-paint.
    6. Place end_block 2x2 in bottom-right bg region, >=1 cell from any path cell.
    7. Paint markers with cycle_colors[0].
    8. Oracle: run solver (asserts path single 4-conn, disjoint trajectories, marker embedded in col-0 path segment, etc).
